{
  "package": "testing",
  "notes": "Go's testing package: T, B, F, M, PB and the TB trait with Go's report format (--- FAIL lines, indented logs, === RUN/PAUSE/CONT/NAME/ATTR in verbose mode, benchmark result lines), usable from Rust #[test] functions through testing::run_test and the test_fn! macro or as a whole test binary through main_start/M::run. Fatal, FailNow, Skip and SkipNow unwind with the Goexit payload (testing::is_goexit). Log/Error/Fatal/Skip take a slice of Display operands (fmt.Sprintln) and the *f forms take format_args!. Subtests: T::run runs inline (may borrow), T::run_static on a thread (parallel). Cleanup closures are 'static. Differences are recorded as deviations; allocation statistics need an allocator calling testing::record_alloc.",
